WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:08.469
Tessera: agents pay each other over x402 into an escrow on Solana, and with 2.0 they can buy now, pay later.

00:08.469 --> 00:12.331
This is the live site, reading devnet in the browser.

00:13.500 --> 00:17.958
The x402 exact scheme on Solana allows only a plain token transfer.

00:17.958 --> 00:27.674
So the merchant quotes the escrow order's account as pay-to: the money lands in its vault, and the program trusts that balance, not anyone's word.

00:28.800 --> 00:31.772
Here is a real 402 from a merchant on devnet.

00:31.772 --> 00:40.753
One order, three ways to pay it: exact, through either of two facilitators, or tessera-paylater, with this buyer's credit limit and fee.

00:40.753 --> 00:42.999
Every option pays into the escrow.

00:44.100 --> 00:45.510
New in 2.0, pay later.

00:45.510 --> 00:52.114
The buyer signs one buy_now at the quoted price, and the merchant checks it, signs it too and sends it.

00:52.114 --> 00:57.435
In that one instruction the pool pays the order's vault and the escrow confirms it.

00:57.435 --> 00:59.486
The buyer repays the pool later.

01:00.600 --> 01:02.034
A real run on devnet.

01:02.034 --> 01:08.314
Nova buys a summary on credit, in one transaction signed by Nova and by Quill, the merchant.

01:08.314 --> 01:12.751
The summary arrives, its hash matches, and the money is released.

01:12.751 --> 01:15.140
Nova repays, and its limit goes up.

01:15.140 --> 01:18.690
Charlie, a new wallet, is refused and signs nothing.

01:19.800 --> 01:30.357
And that transaction, read back from devnet: three signers, the pay-later program's buy now, the pool's transfer, and inside it, the escrow's confirm funded.

01:31.500 --> 01:33.941
When a payment fails, no money is stuck.

01:33.941 --> 01:35.955
A refused payment was never sent.

01:35.955 --> 01:39.738
A settlement left pending is watched until it lands or cannot.

01:39.738 --> 01:46.572
On devnet, a merchant that never delivered was refunded, and disputed deliveries were judged against their hash.

01:46.572 --> 01:49.013
An unpaid loan freezes the buyer's line.

01:50.200 --> 01:55.437
A person can buy from the same agents on the website, with a built-in devnet test wallet.

01:55.437 --> 02:01.028
The merchant opens the escrow, and the browser checks it on-chain before paying into its vault.

02:01.028 --> 02:06.265
The merchant delivers and commits a hash, and the browser checks what arrived against it.

02:06.265 --> 02:10.149
This buyer is new, so the money is held until it confirms receipt.

02:32.200 --> 02:35.349
New this week: an agent that holds no key can still buy.

02:35.349 --> 02:39.117
It asks, and its owner approves on this page from their own wallet.

02:39.117 --> 02:44.572
The page reads the order from the chain and checks it against the link before paying into escrow.

02:44.572 --> 02:48.733
The agent collects the delivery, and the owner keeps the right to dispute.

03:08.200 --> 03:15.425
Every wallet has a credit file anyone can read: the score, what it is made of, and every review with the weight it carried.
